  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support education &amp; conservation with ecobursaries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arabuko-Sokoke Forest and Mida Creek (Kenya) support some of Africa&apos;s rarest wildlife. But as communities fight for survival, they resort to unsustainable exploitation of their local ecosystem. ASSETS is a pioneering community conservation project that lifts children out of poverty through secondary school bursaries and engages families in ecotourism and practical conservation activities. With 775 students sponsored, ASSETS has a proven track-record of success. Help sponsor 100 students in 2024!</narrative>
  </description>
